          <li><strong>Real business facts</strong> (name, address, hours, license) in a form Google and ChatGPT can read. This is the fix that touches the profile. Those facts have to agree on the site and on the profile, because the profile is one of the places Google and AI assistants read them.</li>
          <li><strong>Services listed consistently.</strong> The profile's service list and the site's service list should name the same work. A profile that lists work the site does not sell is a facts problem, not a category trick.</li>
          <li><strong>One buyer guide on the domain.</strong> The guide lives on the site. It is not a purchased profile post.</li>
          <li><strong>Junk pages hidden from search, and one call-or-book button on every page.</strong> Site work. The button is how a visitor acts once they are on the site. This install does not answer the phone.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          The $497 a month keeps every new page titled, readable, and on one
          button, and it updates business facts when they change. Updating
          those facts includes the profile. The three access grants include
          it, and the facts have to stay in agreement. That is maintenance. It
          is not a rankings retainer.
        </p>

